01132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501201 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86542" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501201 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501201 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{y}}{yx}.$ What is the rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=⟨2,4⟩?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501201 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a3fef551-e9bd-56f6-a5fb-6131de39b9cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501201 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of $v$ is equal to the directional derivative ${g}_{u}^{′}(1,1).$ \n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}⟨2,4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient $∇g(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{e}^{y}}{yx}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{e}^{y}}{yx})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{{e}^{y}}{{x}^{2}y},\\,\\frac{{e}^{y}(y-1)}{x{y}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ ∇g(1,1) & =⟨-\\frac{{e}^{1}}{{1}^{2}\\cdot 1},\\,\\frac{{e}^{1}\\cdot (1-1)}{1\\cdot {1}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-e,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the directional derivative ${g}_{u}^{′}(1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =∇g(1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨-e,0⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}(-e\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{e}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{e\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501247 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501247 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0a60e94a-7f5d-54b3-9400-bd9ba416bdb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501247 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186501201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501275 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501275 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7cf532da-0f94-51c8-af70-